{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "25", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "04", "M": "27", "S": "15"}}, "news": [{"title": "Over 800 unauthorised buildings identified across Cyberabad civic body limits", "para": "The Cyberabad Municipal Corporation has uncovered more than 800 unauthorized constructions across its three zones, with Kukatpally zone showing the highest number at 365 violations. Enforcement measures, including show-cause notices, demolitions, and seizures, have been initiated. Many building owners exploit loopholes to bypass regulations. The civic body strongly encourages residents to report any violations via the My CURE app.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/over-800-unauthorised-buildings-identified-across-cyberabad-civic-body-limits/133491269?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-217242/133491269.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Two Parsi bungalows in Mumbai's Perry Cross Road to make way for luxury towers", "para": "Two Parsi-owned bungalows in Bandra's Perry Cross Road will be demolished. Supreme Universal plans to build two luxury towers on the prime one-acre plot. The sale potential of this significant coastal development is estimated at Rs 1,500 crore.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/two-parsi-bungalows-in-mumbais-perry-cross-road-to-make-way-for-luxury-towers/133490535?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-423950/133490535.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "DTCP issues 1,300 fresh notices, over 600 restoration orders in Gurugram", "para": "The Department of Town and Country Planning in Gurgaon is ramping up its enforcement actions. Established residential neighborhoods are now facing show-cause notices and restoration orders as part of a crackdown on unauthorized construction and commercial property misuse. Ongoing demolition and sealing activities are ongoing citywide, emphasizing the necessity for property owners to conform to sanctioned plans and proper land utilization.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/dtcp-issues-1300-fresh-notices-over-600-restoration-orders-in-gurugram/133490075?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-240054/133490075.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}